  "finalText": "Reservation R3311 is cancelled, but you're getting $248.00 in travel credit, not $248 back on your card.\n\n- **Why it's credit:** Your basic economy fare is non-refundable on its own. Your trip insurance does override that. But the insurance only pays back to your card if you cancel at least 14 days before departure. The refund system's date for this booking is 2026-07-28, which is 8 days before the 2026-08-05 flight. Inside that window, the insurance turns the fare into travel credit instead.\n- **Fee:** The $50 cancellation service fee is waived because you're a platinum member. The credit is the full $248.00.\n- **What I did:** I cancelled R3311, which released the seat, and made one ledger entry (L1) for $248.00 in travel credit. I changed no other booking or record.\n- **Date discrepancy:** My task context gave today's date as 2026-10-06, but the refund policy for this booking used 2026-07-28. I followed the policy date, and the flight was still scheduled.",
